  "fix": {
    "fix_type": "restructure",
    "target_module": "simple_spi",
    "added_latency_cycles": 0,
    "modified_rtl": "  always @(posedge clk_i)\n    if(spe & (|clkcnt & |state))\n      // Restructure: split the 12-bit decrement into two 6-bit ripple\n      // blocks with a carry-select on the upper half so the borrow no\n      // longer ripples through all 12 bits. Value is unchanged:\n      // still (clkcnt - 1) mod 4096, including the 0 -> 0xFFF wrap.\n      clkcnt <= { (~|clkcnt[5:0]) ? (clkcnt[11:6] - 6'h1) : clkcnt[11:6],\n                  clkcnt[5:0] - 6'h1 };\n    else\n      case (espr) // synopsys full_case parallel_case\n        4'b0000: clkcnt <= 12'h0;   // 2   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0001: clkcnt <= 12'h1;   // 4   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0010: clkcnt <= 12'h3;   // 16  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0011: clkcnt <= 12'hf;   // 32  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0100: clkcnt <= 12'h1f;  // 8\n        4'b0101: clkcnt <= 12'h7;   // 64\n        4'b0110: clkcnt <= 12'h3f;  // 128\n        4'b0111: clkcnt <= 12'h7f;  // 256\n        4'b1000: clkcnt <= 12'hff;  // 512\n        4'b1001: clkcnt <= 12'h1ff; // 1024\n        4'b1010: clkcnt <= 12'h3ff; // 2048\n        4'b1011: clkcnt <= 12'h7ff; // 4096\n        default : clkcnt <= 12'hfff;\n      endcase",
    "rationale": "The path runs DFF(clkcnt bit) -> 17 unattributed combinational cells (alternating AOI21/INV borrow-generate groups, NAND2/AND2/NOR2/OAI21 propagation, a terminal XOR2) -> DFF(clkcnt bit). The only arithmetic in the shown scope is `clkcnt <= clkcnt - 11'h1`, so this is the borrow-ripple of the SPI clock-divider decrement feeding back into the same clkcnt register.\n\nStrategy = RESTRUCTURE. The 12-bit ripple decrement is rewritten as two 6-bit sub-blocks with carry-select on the upper half: the low block does `clkcnt[5:0]-1`, its borrow-out is `~|clkcnt[5:0]` (a 2-level 6-input NOR tree instead of a 6-deep borrow ripple), and the upper 6 bits are muxed between `clkcnt[11:6]` and `clkcnt[11:6]-1`. This cuts the worst chain from ~12 serial ripple levels to ~6 levels + NOR tree + one mux, using gates no wider than those already on the path, which covers the 0.03 ns shortfall. Provably identical: for clkcnt[5:0] != 0 the result is {U, L-1} with no upper borrow; for clkcnt[5:0] == 0 the low block wraps to 0x3F and the upper block decrements, giving {U-1 mod 64, 0x3F}, i.e. exactly (clkcnt-1) mod 4096 including the 0 -> 0xFFF case. The `espr` constant-load branch is left byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nRETIME rejected: this is a register->comb->same-register feedback loop; there is no register inside the combinational chain (report shows both sequential cells are the path endpoints), so no existing register can be moved to shorten the loop.\n\nPIPELINE rejected: adding a register in the decrement feedback would make clkcnt update every second cycle, changing the SPI clock divide ratio, and the counter reconverges with the `|clkcnt & |state` enable and the downstream clock-generation FSM which are outside this scope and cannot be re-balanced here.\n\nNo reconvergent paths need delaying because latency is unchanged (added_latency_cycles = 0)."
